# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_9648> (tramadol)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_9648> "A racemate consisting of equal amounts of (<i>R</i>,<i>R</i>)- and (<i>S</i>,<i>S</i>)-tramadol. A centrally acting synthetic opioid analgesic, used (as the hydrochloride salt) to treat moderately severe pain. The (<i>R</i>,<i>R</i>)-enantiomer exhibits ten-fold higher analgesic potency than the (<i>S</i>,<i>S</i>)-enantiomer. Originally developed by Grünenthal GmbH and launched in 1977, it was subsequently isolated from the root bark of the South African tree <em>Nauclea latifolia</em>.")
